  "subject": "Every decision dispatch field that names the operator (matches /operator/i) in the decisions files under docs/evidence at base 8c28f479, read 2026-09-29: 241 of 986 decisions. The order counted 228 of 928 at 5f3849ec; 13 were filed since.",
  "rule": "The class is the first operator step the dispatch names, reading left to right. A leading scope expand: or operator override: prefix is the first step. A mention of the operator that is not a step is skipped; a step the text marks as prior, standing or cited (continued under or after, within, standing, default, recorded, a decision reference such as D007 or (WO-167-D008)) is a reference, not a step. With no step the class is none.",
  "classes": {
    "correction": "the operator corrected the agent: named a correction, rejected something, pointed out an error, or clarified or refined what was meant",
    "direction": "the operator instructed, required, requested, directed, steered, permitted, approved or authorized something on their own initiative",
    "scope-expansion": "the operator expanded the scope of the order",
    "override": "the operator used or authorized an override, or overrode a hold",
    "takeover": "the operator took over a stopped or failed session",
    "answer": "the operator answered a question or choice the agent put: answered, response, replied, selected, chose, confirmed, or a picked option label",
    "other-step": "an operator step outside the six: a question, ideation messages, a report, a note, a live attempt the operator ran",
    "none": "no step the operator took: the dispatch label itself, a section name, a reference to a standing or earlier step, an act of the executor, or a model the operator selected"
  },
